WEBVTT

00:04:59.738 --> 00:05:01.500
and with authority.

00:05:02.445 --> 00:05:03.812
That's register.

00:05:04.134 --> 00:05:05.477
Then we have timbre.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.246
It's the way your voice feels.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.602
Again, the research shows

00:05:08.626 --> 00:05:12.400
that we prefer voices
which are rich, smooth, warm,

00:05:12.424 --> 00:05:13.910
like hot chocolate.

00:05:14.635 --> 00:05:17.899
Well if that's not you,
that's not the end of the world,

00:05:17.923 --> 00:05:19.341
because you can train.

00:05:19.365 --> 00:05:20.585
Go and get a voice coach.

00:05:20.609 --> 00:05:22.467
And there are amazing things you can do

00:05:22.491 --> 00:05:24.897
with breathing, with posture,
and with exercises

00:05:24.921 --> 00:05:27.411
to improve the timbre of your voice.

00:05:27.435 --> 00:05:29.203
Then prosody. I love prosody.

00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:31.379
This is the sing-song, the meta-language